.TITLE "man"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Displays the system reference manuals. It provides access to the __documentation__ for terminal commands, system calls, and configuration files.

.DIV "ALIAS"

.DIV "TLDR"
**man command**
Displays the manual page for a specific command.
> __command__ the target tool name

**man -k keyword**
Searches the manual page descriptions for a specific keyword.
> __-k__ keyword search flag

**man -f command**
Displays a short description of what a command does.
> __-f__ whatis flag

**man 5 configuration_file**
Opens the manual page for a specific section, such as configuration files.
> __5__ section number

.DIV "SUMMARY"
The __man__ system is the primary source of truth for command behavior on macOS. When reading a manual, use the __/ __ key to search for specific text and the __q__ key to exit the viewer.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**mac:whatis** **mac:apropos**

documentation: __https://ss64.com/osx/man.html__
